  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In Unity you can disable the Skin Mesh Renders's ability to receive and cast shadows. If possible adding an option in the System menu that can force all avatars to not be able to receive or cast shadows would improve performance. If that option could be extended to disabling shadows in all worlds without baked lighting that would be even better. Not sure if overriding the lighting settings of worlds is possible however as most people don't seem to use the \"User's Settings\" option under shadow Quality.",
